#### Timer Resource Leak in `withTimeout`

The `withTimeout` function sets a timeout but does not clear it if the wrapped promise resolves or rejects before the timeout fires. This can lead to a resource leak, as the timer will remain active until it expires, even if it is no longer needed.

**Recommended Solution:**
Wrap the original promise so that when it settles (either resolves or rejects), `clearTimeout(timeout)` is called. For example:

```typescript
return Promise.race([
  promise.finally(() => clearTimeout(timeout)),
  new Promise<T>((_, reject) => {
    controller.signal.addEventListener("abort", () => {
      clearTimeout(timeout);
      reject(new Error(`Request timeout after ${timeoutMs}ms`));
    });
  })
]);
```
This ensures the timer is always cleared, preventing resource leaks.

